// error
// The bound on #1421's carve-out: `ptrOf` is admitted for its ADDRESS
// computation, not for its operand. The argument stays subject to the §10.3.1
// allowlist exactly as an `asm` operand does, so a slice literal here — which
// allocates — is still E0075. Without this case the carve-out could silently
// widen into "anything written inside ptrOf() is fine".
@nosplit function f(): i64 {
  return atomicLoad(ptrOf([]i64(1)))
}
